---
description: The agent that implements a change does not review it
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not review your own change.
- Hand UX, architecture, security, database, compliance, tests, performance, QA,
  and code quality to the readonly agents: `ux-reviewer`,
  `security-reviewer-baseline`, `security-reviewer-hardening`,
  `database-reviewer`, `compliance-reviewer`, `tests-planner`,
  `performance-reviewer`, `qa`, and `code-reviewer`.
- Specialist implementers (`frontend-engineer`, `backend-engineer`,
  `performance-implementer`, `security-implementer`, `database-implementer`,
  `compliance-implementer`, `tests-writer`, `infrastructure`, `devops`,
  `observability`) never review their own diffs.
- Dispatch readonly reviews proportionally to risk tier and scoped to changed files:
  Tier 0 uses `qa` + `code-reviewer`; Tier 1 adds `security-reviewer-baseline` and
  specialists matching `git diff`; Tier 2 and CRITICAL run the full specialist suite
  and `/ship-check`.
- Find failures before suggesting improvements.
- Do not set Status to accepted on an intent, experience, spec, plan, ADR,
  architecture gate, orchestration log, or debt record.
- The orchestrator may sequence roles and must not be the builder or the approver.
